{# Go supplemental fixture template — emits one
adapters/{bidder}/{bidder}test/supplemental/{scenario_kind}.json file
per supported error-path scenario. Kobler-shape-agnostic: every
adapter that uses canonical-go-helpers status handling (or kobler's
legacy-raw 204+other-non-200 form) can use these fixtures unchanged.

The template covers 5 supplemental scenarios that pad coverage with
zero per-adapter customization:

  1. status-204         — no-content path; mockResponse.status=204 with
                          no body, expectedBidResponses=[] and NO
                          expectedMakeBidsErrors. Matches upstream
                          kobler `status-204.json` exactly.

  2. status-400         — bad-request path. mockResponse.status=400,
                          body={}. expectedMakeBidsErrors[0].value =
                          "Unexpected status code: 400. Run with
                          request.debug = 1 for more info" — emitted
                          verbatim by adapters.CheckResponseStatusCode
                          ForErrors() in `prebid-server/adapters/
                          response.go` (canonical-go-helpers). Note: NO
                          trailing period — the canonical helper omits
                          it, while kobler's bespoke legacy-raw branch
                          adds one. Use the canonical form here so
                          fixtures work for the >70%-of-corpus that
                          uses CheckResponseStatusCodeForErrors.

  3. status-404         — other-non-200 path. status=404, body={}.
                          Same error template as status-400 but with
                          404. Emitted as BadServerResponse by
                          CheckResponseStatusCodeForErrors's else-
                          branch. Matches upstream kobler `status-
                          404.json` modulo the trailing-period drift
                          (kobler emits trailing period, canonical
                          helper does not).

  4. no-response-body   — 200-with-null-body path. status=200, body
                          omitted (or `null`). For kobler-shape
                          adapters (`responseData.Body == nil` short-
                          circuit), this returns (nil, nil) — no
                          error, expectedBidResponses=[]. Canonical-
                          helper adapters that don't short-circuit may
                          surface a jsonutil "unexpected end of JSON"
                          error here; for shape-agnosticism we match
                          upstream kobler `no-response-body.json` (no
                          error). Per-adapter overrides handle the
                          divergence.

  5. malformed-body     — 200-with-non-JSON-string-body path. status=
                          200, body="this is not json" (literal JSON
                          string — adapterstest delivers the raw
                          16-byte content `"this is not json"` to the
                          adapter). jsonutil.Unmarshal sees first
                          byte `"` (the opening quote of the JSON-
                          encoded string) and emits the literal error
                          `expect { or n, but found "` —
                          matches upstream kobler `wrong-response-
                          body-type.json`.

Inputs:
  ctx.scenario_kind         : str  — one of "status-204", "status-400",
                                     "status-404", "no-response-body",
                                     "malformed-body". Drives the
                                     body+status+expected-error shape.
  ctx.mock_bid_request      : dict — the BidRequest the harness feeds
                                     to MakeRequests (typically equal
                                     to the exemplary fixture's
                                     mockBidRequest; the error path is
                                     independent of imp shape).
  ctx.uri                   : str  — endpoint URL the adapter resolves
                                     to. Use the canonical
                                     TEST_ENDPOINT pinned by the
                                     port_engine renderer.
  ctx.expected_request_body : dict — what MakeRequests produces. For
                                     passthrough, equals
                                     mock_bid_request.
  ctx.imp_ids               : list[str] — required by adapterstest
                                          framework (F-new-12).

The emitted JSON shape for each scenario_kind matches the upstream
upstream-Go conventions referenced above. Unknown scenario_kind
values render an empty mockResponse + no expectedMakeBidsErrors —
the renderer is expected to validate the kind upstream and reject
unknown values before invoking this template.
#}
{% set kind = ctx.scenario_kind %}
{
  "mockBidRequest": {{ ctx.mock_bid_request | tojson }},
  "httpCalls": [
    {
      "expectedRequest": {
        "uri": {{ ctx.uri | tojson }},
        "body": {{ ctx.expected_request_body | tojson }},
        "impIDs": {{ ctx.imp_ids | tojson }}
      },
      "mockResponse": {
{% if kind == "status-204" %}
        "status": 204
{% elif kind == "status-400" %}
        "status": 400,
        "body": {}
{% elif kind == "status-404" %}
        "status": 404,
        "body": {}
{% elif kind == "no-response-body" %}
        "status": 200
{% elif kind == "malformed-body" %}
        "status": 200,
        "body": "this is not json"
{% endif %}
      }
    }
  ],
{% if kind == "status-204" or kind == "no-response-body" %}
  "expectedBidResponses": []
{% elif kind == "status-400" %}
  "expectedMakeBidsErrors": [
    {
      "value": "Unexpected status code: 400. Run with request.debug = 1 for more info",
      "comparison": "literal"
    }
  ]
{% elif kind == "status-404" %}
  "expectedMakeBidsErrors": [
    {
      "value": "Unexpected status code: 404. Run with request.debug = 1 for more info",
      "comparison": "literal"
    }
  ]
{% elif kind == "malformed-body" %}
  "expectedMakeBidsErrors": [
    {
      "value": "expect { or n, but found \"",
      "comparison": "literal"
    }
  ]
{% else %}
  "expectedBidResponses": []
{% endif %}
}
